1
00:00:05,738 --> 00:00:07,322
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,347 --> 00:00:08,840
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:30,502 --> 00:00:32,668
Yeah, Gyu Min. I'm on my way.

4
00:00:33,097 --> 00:00:36,972
It'll take about ten minutes.
Okay, see you soon.

5
00:01:14,972 --> 00:01:16,722
The coffee just spilled all of a sudden.

6
00:01:17,597 --> 00:01:19,597
I think I barely brushed you.

7
00:01:20,472 --> 00:01:24,556
You fell while trying to dodge me.
I really think I only brushed this bag.

8
00:01:25,472 --> 00:01:28,847
Shouldn't you apologize first?

9
00:01:34,972 --> 00:01:39,514
How could you speed like that
down such a narrow alley?

10
00:01:40,639 --> 00:01:44,181
Yes, I'm sorry. Are you badly hurt?

11
00:01:46,666 --> 00:01:48,071
Do you want to go to the hospital?

12
00:01:51,296 --> 00:01:52,993
Can I get your number?

13
00:01:53,389 --> 00:01:56,038
The way you're moving,
it doesn't look like anything's broken,

14
00:01:56,358 --> 00:01:58,206
and you don't seem badly hurt,

15
00:01:58,231 --> 00:02:03,575
so no claiming later you need admission.
Let's just go to the hospital.

16
00:02:06,737 --> 00:02:09,612
I'm in a hurry to get somewhere,
so I can't go to the hospital.

17
00:02:10,181 --> 00:02:13,931
If anything comes up, I'll call you,
so give me your phone number.

18
00:02:14,847 --> 00:02:17,139
So you can get hurt somewhere else
and say I hit you?

19
00:02:18,181 --> 00:02:20,181
I've seen plenty of people
who fake accidents for money.

20
00:02:22,014 --> 00:02:23,722
Should we go to the police, then?

21
00:02:24,139 --> 00:02:27,597
Want to settle it, then?
Who's the victim and who's at fault?

22
00:02:32,931 --> 00:02:34,597
Wait a minute.

23
00:02:35,889 --> 00:02:38,681
I'm really busy too.

24
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:44,514
The thing is, my father's critically ill,
so I need to get going too.

25
00:02:53,764 --> 00:02:56,056
(Pharmacy)

26
00:03:21,347 --> 00:03:23,347
(Episode 28)

27
00:03:24,139 --> 00:03:25,806
Pick one.

28
00:03:26,181 --> 00:03:29,556
Either throw one of your usual fits
and blame everyone else,

29
00:03:30,347 --> 00:03:33,597
or if you're worried about Gyu Seo,
just say so.

30
00:03:34,972 --> 00:03:38,556
Why would I worry about that brat Gyu Seo?
When did I ever?

31
00:03:41,722 --> 00:03:43,680
There's still some hope after all.

32
00:03:44,487 --> 00:03:47,507
They say people can't change.

33
00:03:49,889 --> 00:03:54,847
Maybe even Han Gyu Yeong can be fixed.

34
00:03:56,306 --> 00:03:58,222
What are you going on about?

35
00:03:59,097 --> 00:04:00,690
Is your phone still off?

36
00:04:00,883 --> 00:04:02,883
Did you check if anything came in?

37
00:04:09,431 --> 00:04:15,097
Sometimes you actually listen.
You're better than a puppy.

38
00:04:22,347 --> 00:04:27,264
Han Gyu Yeong, keep pushing my buttons,
and instead of you, your family...

39
00:04:27,264 --> 00:04:29,889
- What a psycho.
- I'll take them down one by one.

40
00:04:29,972 --> 00:04:31,639
Come home while I'm still being nice.

41
00:04:31,664 --> 00:04:33,914
Why? What is it?

42
00:04:35,056 --> 00:04:38,014
What family? What family do I even have,
that bastard...

43
00:04:38,264 --> 00:04:41,806
I've cut ties with all of them,
so what family do I have?

44
00:05:03,939 --> 00:05:08,314
Hello. You must be new here.

45
00:05:11,639 --> 00:05:15,306
I'm here to help in the kitchen today.

46
00:05:15,431 --> 00:05:16,597
Okay.

47
00:05:17,139 --> 00:05:22,056
Could you take a look and see
what happened to my back and shoulder?

48
00:05:22,087 --> 00:05:25,253
I don't have anyone else to ask...

49
00:05:25,529 --> 00:05:29,054
- Sure.
- Thank you.

50
00:05:35,689 --> 00:05:39,170
What's this? What happened?

51
00:05:40,222 --> 00:05:42,431
I had a little accident on the way here...

52
00:05:46,133 --> 00:05:50,360
I can't reach it,
so could you put a bandage on for me?

53
00:05:50,597 --> 00:05:53,347
Just enough so the blood
doesn't seep through.

54
00:05:56,534 --> 00:05:58,409
That looks really painful.

55
00:06:03,587 --> 00:06:05,647
Shouldn't you go to the hospital?

56
00:06:08,752 --> 00:06:12,752
I'm fine. The chef's on his own,
so I want to hurry back.

57
00:06:13,995 --> 00:06:15,120
There. Done.

58
00:06:21,847 --> 00:06:24,889
Please don't tell anyone I got hurt today.

59
00:06:25,764 --> 00:06:27,056
Thank you.

60
00:06:31,128 --> 00:06:34,003
Why is a kitchen helper
working that hard...

61
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:53,404
I'll do it.

62
00:06:54,681 --> 00:06:55,722
Gyu Rim.

63
00:06:58,722 --> 00:06:59,931
What else can I do?

64
00:07:01,097 --> 00:07:02,889
Just keep doing that.

65
00:07:07,722 --> 00:07:09,847
Don't look at me
with those suspicious eyes.

66
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:13,972
You'll be amazed.

67
00:07:14,014 --> 00:07:15,806
It does look really good, I guess.

68
00:07:16,266 --> 00:07:18,686
I'll have a verdict in under five minutes.

69
00:07:24,056 --> 00:07:25,764
All right, how about a toast?

70
00:07:25,806 --> 00:07:28,347
- Sure.
- Thank you.

71
00:07:28,418 --> 00:07:31,252
- Good to see you.
- Thanks for coming.

72
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,872
How is it?

73
00:07:54,259 --> 00:07:56,217
The flavor is out of this world.

74
00:07:57,453 --> 00:07:59,203
And this sea bream's from Wando too?

75
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,982
It came in this morning at dawn,
I'm telling you.

76
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:05,412
- It's really good.
- I just found a great restaurant.

77
00:08:06,865 --> 00:08:08,309
So refreshing.

78
00:08:09,303 --> 00:08:11,753
You're starting a live stream?

79
00:08:13,931 --> 00:08:15,264
Hello, everyone.

80
00:08:15,597 --> 00:08:19,514
Today, on a friend's recommendation,
I'm trying a very special dish.

81
00:08:19,806 --> 00:08:24,514
It's red sea bream capellini
from a restaurant called Da Solo.

82
00:08:25,806 --> 00:08:28,431
They say this sea bream is from Wando too.

83
00:08:30,029 --> 00:08:32,904
Chairman Oh looks a lot livelier
since he started broadcasting.

84
00:08:34,275 --> 00:08:35,806
Is it doing well?

85
00:08:37,056 --> 00:08:40,472
- His channel's crazy popular.
- Really?

86
00:08:40,497 --> 00:08:47,163
Young people go wild over it, and he just
got a gold badge or something recently.

87
00:08:50,597 --> 00:08:56,847
The oil comes through rich and nutty,
and the chewy sea bream and the springy...

88
00:08:57,264 --> 00:09:00,097
- capellini, the combination...
- Hold on.

89
00:09:00,764 --> 00:09:02,597
I just turn this, right? Okay.

90
00:09:02,889 --> 00:09:04,889
Sorry to interrupt the broadcast.

91
00:09:05,097 --> 00:09:10,431
I'm Jang Hun Tae,
the one who introduced Da Solo today.

92
00:09:11,556 --> 00:09:13,097
I'm the CEO of Seonga Apparel.

93
00:09:13,389 --> 00:09:15,972
As for Chairman Oh here today,

94
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:19,597
he seems to be exaggerating quite a bit,
so let me be honest with you.

95
00:09:19,786 --> 00:09:24,661
The capellini here is just not good.

96
00:09:26,503 --> 00:09:31,264
I've had plenty of experience abroad,
and as someone with a refined palate,

97
00:09:31,289 --> 00:09:35,409
I'd say the food here is a joke.

98
00:09:36,002 --> 00:09:38,127
Yes, I just don't recommend it.

99
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,843
There's no need to come here. Really.

100
00:09:41,764 --> 00:09:46,416
Just never come here, okay?

101
00:09:55,864 --> 00:09:59,864
Mu Jin, why are you shaking so much?

102
00:10:04,014 --> 00:10:05,764
It's okay. You did great.

103
00:10:06,306 --> 00:10:09,889
You did so well,
there's nothing more you could've done.

104
00:10:11,648 --> 00:10:12,889
Thank you.

105
00:10:41,608 --> 00:10:43,762
Four point eight out of five.

106
00:10:44,014 --> 00:10:50,306
The 0.2 deduction is for serving mistakes
by Jang Seo Hyeon, a last-minute fill-in.

107
00:10:56,681 --> 00:10:58,514
Gyu Rim, are you okay?

108
00:10:58,639 --> 00:11:01,139
Yeah, the tension just drained out of me.

109
00:11:06,097 --> 00:11:10,139
I kept my promise, right? I won it all.

110
00:11:13,157 --> 00:11:14,490
Yes, it's not good.

111
00:11:14,722 --> 00:11:17,847
I've lived abroad in all kinds of places,

112
00:11:17,889 --> 00:11:21,931
and I've got a refined palate,
so let me say it again.

113
00:11:22,244 --> 00:11:23,786
This place is a joke.

114
00:11:24,389 --> 00:11:26,472
Yes, I just don't recommend it.

115
00:11:26,972 --> 00:11:29,056
There's no need to come here. Really.

116
00:11:30,097 --> 00:11:35,347
Just never come here. There's no need.

117
00:11:35,389 --> 00:11:37,222
- Yes.
- What are you doing?

118
00:11:38,181 --> 00:11:41,461
Hey, are you scared too many people
will come to your regular spot?

119
00:11:41,661 --> 00:11:45,161
Yes. I want to enjoy a place like this
all to myself. So what?

120
00:11:45,237 --> 00:11:48,445
Once it's on air, people flock here,
and it gets chaotic.

121
00:11:48,470 --> 00:11:51,470
Then I lose another one
of my secret hideouts.

122
00:11:51,953 --> 00:11:53,953
It's on air right now.

123
00:11:56,009 --> 00:11:59,256
It's on air? Seriously...

124
00:11:59,494 --> 00:12:05,515
Well, you're welcome to come, but please
don't spread the word. I'm begging you.

125
00:12:05,764 --> 00:12:08,222
- Don't spread the word.
- Come by.

126
00:12:08,247 --> 00:12:11,289
- Don't spread the word, I'm begging you.
- Okay.

127
00:12:12,097 --> 00:12:13,847
What is he doing right now?

128
00:12:15,889 --> 00:12:19,722
Why is he lying?
Since when is he a regular?

129
00:12:20,776 --> 00:12:24,556
He must've wanted to help since
Mu Jin's restaurant is struggling.

130
00:12:25,556 --> 00:12:28,722
He sure sticks his nose in everything.

131
00:12:29,139 --> 00:12:30,538
Who does he think he is?

132
00:12:30,563 --> 00:12:33,458
He wrecked a 40-year friendship,
so who does he think he is?

133
00:12:43,566 --> 00:12:47,066
Who am I? Where am I?

134
00:12:49,472 --> 00:12:50,639
Good work, kiddo.

135
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,840
Didn't I tell you
I'm not middle-school Jang Seo Hyeon?

136
00:12:55,472 --> 00:12:58,181
Sorry, I'm really sorry.

137
00:12:59,467 --> 00:13:01,708
What do you take me for?

138
00:13:01,962 --> 00:13:03,556
Who rubs a girl's head like that...

139
00:13:03,581 --> 00:13:05,998
Am I your army junior?
Am I that easy to push around?

140
00:13:06,181 --> 00:13:08,015
You're anything but easy to push around.

141
00:13:08,639 --> 00:13:12,847
There was a time when just looking at you
made my heart pound like crazy.

142
00:13:13,162 --> 00:13:14,704
What's that supposed to mean?

143
00:13:14,806 --> 00:13:17,389
Didn't I tell you? When I first saw you...

144
00:13:21,056 --> 00:13:24,211
I thought, "How can a girl
be this charming?"

145
00:13:24,878 --> 00:13:26,771
I fell for you at first sight.

146
00:13:28,191 --> 00:13:29,639
You never told me that.

147
00:13:32,014 --> 00:13:33,472
I guess I only said it in my head,

148
00:13:33,514 --> 00:13:37,264
after I found out you were head over heels
for Mu Jin.

149
00:13:39,324 --> 00:13:42,782
You should've at least said it out loud.

150
00:13:44,056 --> 00:13:46,097
Said what?

151
00:13:47,639 --> 00:13:52,181
When I found out you liked Mu Jin,
I got over you in a day. So why would I?

152
00:13:57,844 --> 00:13:59,260
What's with that face?

153
00:14:00,217 --> 00:14:04,042
Anyone would think
you have feelings for me, kid.

154
00:14:05,237 --> 00:14:06,743
Are you crazy?

155
00:14:14,014 --> 00:14:18,431
By the way, that woman helping
in the kitchen, you should pay her well.

156
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:20,121
She didn't even look after herself...

157
00:14:21,847 --> 00:14:23,895
and worked as if it were her own business,

158
00:14:23,968 --> 00:14:26,259
so don't be stingy.
Give her a big bonus too.

159
00:14:26,284 --> 00:14:28,576
Who, the kitchen helper? Gyu Rim?

160
00:14:29,745 --> 00:14:35,815
Gyu Rim? Han Gyu Rim?

161
00:14:37,764 --> 00:14:39,764
Yeah, I just got home.

162
00:14:41,764 --> 00:14:44,722
Thanks, my guardian.

163
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:55,639
Don't think about anything.
Just get some rest tonight.

164
00:14:56,306 --> 00:14:58,097
I'm going to wash up
and go straight to bed too.

165
00:14:59,639 --> 00:15:04,472
Sleep well, and let's meet again
in our dreams. Good night.

166
00:15:05,472 --> 00:15:06,597
Good night.

167
00:15:13,972 --> 00:15:15,722
Get up, Kim Mu Jin. Wake up!

168
00:15:16,056 --> 00:15:18,556
I went to bed at 4 a.m.

169
00:15:18,736 --> 00:15:22,806
Amazing. We're fully booked.
Not a single table left.

170
00:15:25,186 --> 00:15:27,603
What are you talking about?
Say that again.

171
00:15:29,407 --> 00:15:32,018
It's been exactly a week
since the Chairman came.

172
00:15:32,556 --> 00:15:33,722
What's going on?

173
00:15:34,097 --> 00:15:37,764
We were never 100 percent booked,
even before.

174
00:15:38,181 --> 00:15:41,056
And next month's already
over 70 percent booked.

175
00:15:41,222 --> 00:15:42,431
No way.

176
00:15:42,639 --> 00:15:44,139
Anyway, we've hit the reset button.

177
00:15:50,597 --> 00:15:53,931
We don't have to close the restaurant.

178
00:15:54,222 --> 00:15:56,139
We don't have to go harvest abalone.

179
00:15:58,014 --> 00:15:59,764
I should tell Gyu Rim too.

180
00:16:01,556 --> 00:16:04,889
Morning to night, it's all Gyu Rim.
Is she all you think about?

181
00:16:05,139 --> 00:16:09,181
Can't you share this joy with me,
the one right here in front of you?

182
00:16:09,222 --> 00:16:10,389
Okay, man.

183
00:16:11,556 --> 00:16:16,472
Yeah, man. They say lovers are temps,
but friends are full-time.

184
00:16:17,556 --> 00:16:18,639
Is that a saying?

185
00:16:19,306 --> 00:16:20,556
Who even says that?

186
00:16:21,014 --> 00:16:25,931
It is. When a lover sulks, you make up.
When a friend sulks, you buy them a meal.

187
00:16:25,972 --> 00:16:27,181
That's a saying too.

188
00:16:27,347 --> 00:16:31,514
A lover costs you time and emotions,
but a friend...

189
00:16:31,556 --> 00:16:33,847
Okay. I'll buy you a meal, my friend.

190
00:16:34,181 --> 00:16:36,468
That's not what I mean.
I mean that friends are...

191
00:16:36,493 --> 00:16:38,284
I'll buy you a really expensive meal.

192
00:16:41,014 --> 00:16:42,764
Gyu Rim, are you up?

193
00:16:46,681 --> 00:16:49,389
Go on, keep looking for Gyu Rim
until the day you die.

194
00:16:51,429 --> 00:16:53,244
Well, that's not much of a curse...

195
00:16:59,039 --> 00:17:00,556
Seriously, this is amazing.

196
00:17:02,556 --> 00:17:06,389
Mu Jin never misses.
It worked out so well, Gyu Rim.

197
00:17:06,847 --> 00:17:09,639
You worked so hard too,
Gyu Min. Thank you.

198
00:17:09,722 --> 00:17:12,264
You worked even harder.

199
00:17:14,552 --> 00:17:16,302
So Mu Jin's doing okay now?

200
00:17:18,014 --> 00:17:20,764
You took off your eye patch.
Is your pink eye all better?

201
00:17:21,014 --> 00:17:23,847
Yeah, of course. It's been a week.

202
00:17:24,402 --> 00:17:25,627
Let me see.

203
00:17:26,687 --> 00:17:28,474
Are you really okay?

204
00:17:28,572 --> 00:17:31,406
Really. Totally. Perfectly fine.

205
00:17:31,431 --> 00:17:34,972
Yeah. Don't worry, Gyu Rim. Don't you know
Han Gyu Seo's monster-level recovery?

206
00:17:35,972 --> 00:17:37,639
He's practically a zombie.

207
00:17:38,722 --> 00:17:41,639
Don't get hurt, Gyu Seo.
It breaks my heart.

208
00:17:42,994 --> 00:17:45,536
Get pink eye one more time,
and you're dead.

209
00:17:46,508 --> 00:17:47,758
Hey.

210
00:17:49,264 --> 00:17:51,597
Gyu Rim, can we talk for a minute?

211
00:17:59,014 --> 00:18:00,347
You got married?

212
00:18:04,639 --> 00:18:05,972
To Gyeol's homeroom teacher?

213
00:18:07,578 --> 00:18:09,286
We're registering our marriage today too.

214
00:18:10,847 --> 00:18:12,931
Can you sign as our witness?

215
00:18:19,355 --> 00:18:24,438
You must be really shocked.
I know you are, but...

216
00:18:28,764 --> 00:18:32,431
It just happened that way. I'm sorry.
Please try to understand.

217
00:18:34,931 --> 00:18:41,889
Okay. You're both adults,
and you must have had your reasons.

218
00:18:44,722 --> 00:18:46,806
Have you told Ms. Kwon's family?

219
00:18:47,385 --> 00:18:51,135
No, not yet. Hui Na said she'd handle it
and asked me to leave it to her.

220
00:18:53,014 --> 00:18:57,472
Still, I hope you tell them
before it's too late.

221
00:18:58,449 --> 00:18:59,490
I will.

222
00:19:05,014 --> 00:19:06,431
Aren't you going to congratulate me?

223
00:19:06,682 --> 00:19:11,876
Right. Congratulations, Gyu O.
I'm happy for you.

224
00:19:12,431 --> 00:19:17,889
You have to take care of Ms. Kwon
no matter what and make her happy, okay?

225
00:19:19,862 --> 00:19:22,822
Of course. That's why I'm marrying her.

226
00:19:24,779 --> 00:19:29,070
Okay, then that's all I need.

227
00:19:31,099 --> 00:19:33,776
Gyu Yeong got married off in such a rush,

228
00:19:33,801 --> 00:19:37,884
so I really wanted to do things right
and give you a proper send-off,

229
00:19:39,232 --> 00:19:44,982
but this is my first time too,
so I'm sorry, Gyu O.

230
00:19:51,431 --> 00:19:53,431
Why do you have such rotten luck, Gyu Rim?

231
00:19:53,706 --> 00:19:57,039
Not a single one of your siblings
is normal.

232
00:19:59,348 --> 00:20:00,800
Not that I'm normal either.

233
00:20:04,181 --> 00:20:09,222
By the way, have you ever
contacted Gyu Yeong?

234
00:20:11,264 --> 00:20:15,014
This here helps prevent dementia,
I'm telling you.

235
00:20:15,764 --> 00:20:18,014
She doesn't have dementia.
It's memory loss.

236
00:20:18,056 --> 00:20:20,722
Dementia, memory loss, poop, feces,
it's all the same.

237
00:20:22,347 --> 00:20:28,097
And there's no scientific proof
that Go-Stop prevents dementia either.

238
00:20:28,347 --> 00:20:30,222
Science, my foot.

239
00:20:30,347 --> 00:20:35,056
Science, you can toss with sesame oil
and eat when you're out of side dishes.

240
00:20:38,931 --> 00:20:40,230
Aren't you going to focus?

241
00:20:40,294 --> 00:20:44,017
Because of you, I'm doing everything
short of playing dead here.

242
00:20:44,806 --> 00:20:49,014
Look here.

243
00:20:49,681 --> 00:20:52,472
This here is a bird,

244
00:20:52,514 --> 00:20:57,681
and like this, you need five birds
to get five points.

245
00:20:57,915 --> 00:21:04,872
And there are Blue Ribbons, Red Ribbons,
and Grass Ribbons...

246
00:21:07,056 --> 00:21:10,722
How can your eyes be like that
the whole week...

247
00:21:10,829 --> 00:21:13,787
Like a donkey that got gassed
by coal briquettes?

248
00:21:14,264 --> 00:21:17,306
She's not interested at all.

249
00:21:17,681 --> 00:21:24,139
Mom, if you really want to play with her,
let's play for money, ten cents a point.

250
00:21:24,677 --> 00:21:27,969
Money? Should we play for money?

251
00:21:34,865 --> 00:21:38,032
So how many Go is this? Five?

252
00:21:38,431 --> 00:21:41,014
How many points is this?

253
00:21:41,181 --> 00:21:43,297
- I shook earlier.
- Shook?

254
00:21:44,847 --> 00:21:47,097
What is it with you? Are you a card shark?

255
00:21:48,681 --> 00:21:50,806
Have you come to your senses?

256
00:21:53,139 --> 00:21:57,472
Gyu Yeong's always been a snob
whose eyes light up at money,

257
00:21:58,472 --> 00:22:00,972
and since she used to be so smart,

258
00:22:01,014 --> 00:22:04,306
her mind must be swinging back and forth
like crazy.

259
00:22:05,029 --> 00:22:07,024
I need to go to the bathroom.

260
00:22:12,474 --> 00:22:18,621
Heung Sik, should I take that girl
to Jeongseon for a round?

261
00:22:18,773 --> 00:22:21,190
- What? Jeongseon?
- Yeah.

262
00:22:21,717 --> 00:22:24,717
By the way, how are your hemorrhoids?

263
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:26,496
All healed?

264
00:22:26,878 --> 00:22:29,295
It's been a week. How is it?

265
00:22:29,764 --> 00:22:32,181
Hey, if you're sitting there, use this.

266
00:22:32,742 --> 00:22:33,950
Hold on.

267
00:22:45,431 --> 00:22:49,722
Han Gyu Yeong, keep pushing my buttons,
and instead of you, your family...

268
00:22:49,764 --> 00:22:51,597
I'll take them down one by one.

269
00:22:52,056 --> 00:22:54,597
Come home while I'm still being nice.

270
00:22:55,306 --> 00:22:57,389
What a psycho, seriously.

271
00:22:59,931 --> 00:23:02,847
Kang Seong Uk,
just try touching my family.

272
00:23:02,924 --> 00:23:05,320
I'll grind you up and drink you down.

273
00:23:20,514 --> 00:23:22,972
My mom must really be getting old.

274
00:23:24,002 --> 00:23:28,877
How could she fall for such clumsy acting
without noticing a thing?

275
00:23:30,889 --> 00:23:32,097
What's with the rose?

276
00:23:32,328 --> 00:23:36,620
This? I picked it up on the street
while carrying Mom's bags.

277
00:23:37,148 --> 00:23:40,273
Why? Do you want it?

278
00:23:42,472 --> 00:23:46,639
If you bought it for me, just say so.
Picked it up on the street, my foot.

279
00:23:47,014 --> 00:23:49,222
Buy flowers for you? Am I crazy?

280
00:23:50,264 --> 00:23:52,264
I even took a picture. Look at this.

281
00:23:53,347 --> 00:23:56,889
See? Can't you see all the roses
spilled all over the street?

282
00:23:57,472 --> 00:23:58,556
Even a picture...

283
00:24:02,306 --> 00:24:05,306
So, nothing from Seong Uk?

284
00:24:06,181 --> 00:24:07,514
That psycho...

285
00:24:09,972 --> 00:24:11,014
Nothing.

286
00:24:11,847 --> 00:24:15,389
If you get worked up and go after him,
you'll just cause more trouble.

287
00:24:15,414 --> 00:24:19,664
Why? What is it?
Did that guy come near our house again?

288
00:24:19,689 --> 00:24:22,357
Forget it. I'll handle my own problems.

289
00:24:25,844 --> 00:24:28,219
Keep being nice, and people think
they're entitled to it,

290
00:24:28,570 --> 00:24:30,737
so stop being so nice to me too.

291
00:24:32,063 --> 00:24:33,690
I'm the type who bites the hand
that feeds me.

292
00:24:34,806 --> 00:24:37,931
Looks like you're really upset
with the Chairman,

293
00:24:38,347 --> 00:24:40,931
but nothing he said was wrong.

294
00:24:41,056 --> 00:24:42,347
Who said it was?

295
00:24:43,036 --> 00:24:46,552
Anyway, stop being nice to me.
I'll just bite the hand that feeds me.

296
00:24:47,139 --> 00:24:49,014
I'm not taking help from anyone anymore.

297
00:24:57,509 --> 00:25:01,425
I'm so sorry. I told my mom everything.

298
00:25:02,139 --> 00:25:06,889
I told her I went to see you,
that I asked for your help, all of it.

299
00:25:07,889 --> 00:25:09,431
I'm really sorry.

300
00:25:09,889 --> 00:25:14,097
No. You didn't do anything wrong,
so don't apologize. You did good.

301
00:25:15,139 --> 00:25:18,222
Okay, got it. Hold on.

302
00:25:18,972 --> 00:25:20,972
Hey, I think your mom's
already stormed in.

303
00:25:21,639 --> 00:25:25,181
I'll handle it, so don't worry. Okay.

304
00:25:28,191 --> 00:25:30,968
- Yes?
- Chairwoman Hong is here.

305
00:25:31,629 --> 00:25:32,856
Well, then...

306
00:25:32,931 --> 00:25:36,306
Hey, you want to fight me or what?

307
00:25:38,264 --> 00:25:39,847
You're not normal right now.

308
00:25:40,514 --> 00:25:43,431
I don't talk to people who aren't normal,
so just leave for now.

309
00:25:43,455 --> 00:25:44,455
Hey!

310
00:25:46,682 --> 00:25:47,682
Actually, no.

311
00:25:49,271 --> 00:25:51,192
Come to the hospital with me.

312
00:25:51,495 --> 00:25:53,928
I think you need counseling right now.

313
00:25:54,115 --> 00:25:55,886
I'll go with you, so let's go.

314
00:25:56,007 --> 00:25:58,328
- Come on.
- Let go!

315
00:25:58,781 --> 00:26:00,468
Hey, who do you think you are?

316
00:26:00,655 --> 00:26:02,846
Who are you to meddle
in my family business?

317
00:26:02,871 --> 00:26:04,218
Do you have nothing better to do?

318
00:26:04,755 --> 00:26:07,102
It's not someone else's business.
It's my daughter's.

319
00:26:07,622 --> 00:26:10,047
- What?
- Gyu Rim is my daughter.

320
00:26:10,922 --> 00:26:13,629
Did you do all those crazy things
to separate Mu Jin and Gyu Rim?

321
00:26:15,455 --> 00:26:18,571
If I didn't know, fine, but now that I do,
should I just sit back and do nothing?

322
00:26:19,083 --> 00:26:23,150
Hey! How is she your daughter?

323
00:26:24,015 --> 00:26:25,534
Have you ever met Han Gyu Rim?

324
00:26:25,768 --> 00:26:27,748
Has she ever called you Dad?

325
00:26:27,955 --> 00:26:31,447
You never even saw her face in 33 years,
so what kind of nonsense is this?

326
00:26:31,449 --> 00:26:33,461
What's wrong with you?

327
00:26:34,354 --> 00:26:35,561
How did you end up like this?

328
00:26:36,251 --> 00:26:38,404
Why do you keep being unreasonable
and throwing tantrums?

329
00:26:38,429 --> 00:26:40,129
Are you some spoiled, sulky kid?

330
00:26:41,439 --> 00:26:43,228
Where did it all go wrong for you?

331
00:26:44,095 --> 00:26:48,671
Ok Seon, just admit it when you're wrong.

332
00:26:49,178 --> 00:26:52,322
If your brakes are broken,
grip the wheel and try to stop.

333
00:26:52,323 --> 00:26:54,349
Why do you keep stepping on the gas?

334
00:26:54,395 --> 00:26:55,715
How far are you planning to go?

335
00:26:55,895 --> 00:26:58,008
- All that's at the end is a cliff!
- Hey!

336
00:27:00,195 --> 00:27:04,210
Look at you, doing things you never do.

337
00:27:04,859 --> 00:27:10,234
Hey, you think I put Mu Jin through
all that tough business education...

338
00:27:10,259 --> 00:27:12,122
just so he'd be a chef
at some two-bit restaurant?

339
00:27:12,648 --> 00:27:16,890
You think I raised him like a treasure
so he'd reject all those amazing women...

340
00:27:16,915 --> 00:27:18,794
and end up with a nobody like her?

341
00:27:18,831 --> 00:27:20,149
Watch your mouth.

342
00:27:20,242 --> 00:27:25,332
I'm going to drag Mu Jin
all the way down to rock bottom.

343
00:27:25,383 --> 00:27:28,141
So he'll regret it, crying tears of blood!

344
00:27:28,202 --> 00:27:32,578
So he'll come crawling back to my company.

345
00:27:32,760 --> 00:27:36,161
Not Kim Mu Jin,
the owner of a local restaurant,

346
00:27:36,231 --> 00:27:41,078
but Kim Mu Jin, chairman of Dongyun Group,
known to the whole world.

347
00:27:41,273 --> 00:27:43,008
No matter what!

348
00:27:54,375 --> 00:27:55,762
Thank you.

349
00:28:15,615 --> 00:28:16,898
Hey, it's me.

350
00:28:18,059 --> 00:28:19,059
Yeah.

351
00:28:20,115 --> 00:28:22,249
About the seafood you supply to Da Solo.

352
00:28:23,391 --> 00:28:24,988
Are you on your way to ship it now?

353
00:28:25,175 --> 00:28:26,769
They're using it for tonight's dinner?

354
00:28:32,062 --> 00:28:34,389
I heard your factory investment
completely tanked.

355
00:28:34,524 --> 00:28:37,518
I've heard you're borrowing money
all over the place. Is that true?

356
00:28:38,556 --> 00:28:40,296
(Special Dinner Featuring Fresh
Geumyeong Bay Oysters from Clean Seas)

357
00:28:41,075 --> 00:28:43,355
Yeah. I'm making oyster dishes today.

358
00:28:44,674 --> 00:28:47,164
You love raw oysters.
Come by and eat later.

359
00:28:49,094 --> 00:28:51,825
Of course. The sous-chef
started yesterday,

360
00:28:51,850 --> 00:28:54,923
and the assistant chefs and staff
are getting more in sync.

361
00:28:57,289 --> 00:29:01,131
But Gyu Rim, don't you miss me?

362
00:29:01,795 --> 00:29:04,622
It's already been four days
since we last saw each other.

363
00:29:05,345 --> 00:29:09,115
I've missed you like crazy.
My eyes are sore from waiting.

364
00:29:12,736 --> 00:29:14,102
I mean it.

365
00:29:14,492 --> 00:29:17,320
(Suragan Side Dishes)

366
00:29:17,322 --> 00:29:18,322
Okay.

367
00:29:18,957 --> 00:29:21,110
Let's see each other after work today.

368
00:29:21,825 --> 00:29:23,780
Yeah. I'll call you.

369
00:29:26,748 --> 00:29:30,607
- Su Nam!
- Yeah. Back from a delivery?

370
00:29:30,632 --> 00:29:34,037
- Su Nam!
- Yeah.

371
00:29:35,207 --> 00:29:37,915
Do you know you've been acting
really weird lately?

372
00:29:38,182 --> 00:29:40,409
Me? How?

373
00:29:40,595 --> 00:29:44,934
You get startled every time you see me,
and you seem to avoid my eyes.

374
00:29:45,189 --> 00:29:47,508
What do you mean, startled?

375
00:29:47,761 --> 00:29:49,048
I wasn't avoiding you.

376
00:29:49,195 --> 00:29:51,886
I'm looking right at you like this.

377
00:29:53,728 --> 00:29:55,996
Okay. I guess I was mistaken.

378
00:29:56,222 --> 00:29:58,069
I just missed the way you look at me.

379
00:29:59,817 --> 00:30:03,015
- Your phone's ringing. Answer it.
- Okay.

380
00:30:06,708 --> 00:30:07,764
Hello?

381
00:30:07,990 --> 00:30:11,661
- Is this Han Gyu Rim's phone?
- Yes, it is.

382
00:30:14,068 --> 00:30:15,794
This is Jang Seo Hyeon.

383
00:30:16,448 --> 00:30:18,784
I got your number from Jeong Woo.

384
00:30:20,488 --> 00:30:23,621
A week ago, in the restroom at Da Solo,

385
00:30:24,473 --> 00:30:27,694
I put medicine on the cut on your back
and taped gauze over it.

386
00:30:29,895 --> 00:30:30,895
Hi.

387
00:30:44,715 --> 00:30:46,578
How's your back?

388
00:30:47,153 --> 00:30:48,816
Did you go to the hospital?

389
00:30:49,605 --> 00:30:52,807
Yes. Thanks so much for the other day.

390
00:30:56,548 --> 00:31:00,236
By any chance, Jang Seo Hyeon...

391
00:31:01,891 --> 00:31:03,987
Have you ever heard my name?

392
00:31:06,428 --> 00:31:07,606
No.

393
00:31:10,361 --> 00:31:13,471
I've heard a lot about you, though.

394
00:31:15,290 --> 00:31:16,689
About me?

395
00:31:22,408 --> 00:31:23,997
My mother's name is...

396
00:31:27,185 --> 00:31:28,302
Ko Yun Hui.

397
00:31:37,394 --> 00:31:39,921
That's right.
The person you're thinking of.

398
00:31:41,834 --> 00:31:45,521
The woman who gave birth to you.
The woman who raised me.

399
00:31:54,167 --> 00:31:58,096
I heard you called my mom seven years ago.

400
00:32:00,002 --> 00:32:02,401
And that you changed
your number after that.

401
00:32:05,635 --> 00:32:07,273
I heard about it.

402
00:32:08,774 --> 00:32:12,133
That you called her ten years
after you two were separated.

403
00:32:14,314 --> 00:32:16,297
You asked her to come just once,

404
00:32:18,009 --> 00:32:19,588
but she couldn't because of me.

405
00:32:22,022 --> 00:32:27,235
After my appendix surgery,
she was nursing me and couldn't go to you.

406
00:32:33,349 --> 00:32:37,093
I think Mom's going to divorce Dad.

407
00:32:44,668 --> 00:32:46,984
There's a guy I like,

408
00:32:48,217 --> 00:32:49,671
but Mom was against it,

409
00:32:50,854 --> 00:32:56,421
and I was so angry and bitter,
I told her to get out of our house.

410
00:33:00,334 --> 00:33:02,776
She didn't go even when her own daughter
begged her to come,

411
00:33:03,277 --> 00:33:05,194
and she lived only for me.

412
00:33:06,851 --> 00:33:08,888
She loved me a thousand times more...

413
00:33:08,890 --> 00:33:11,148
than my birth mother ever did.

414
00:33:14,082 --> 00:33:16,662
What kind of awful girl am I?

415
00:33:18,288 --> 00:33:20,206
All over some guy.

416
00:33:26,029 --> 00:33:27,889
I don't even feel human.

417
00:33:29,430 --> 00:33:31,495
I'm really going to pay for this.

418
00:33:36,088 --> 00:33:40,826
When I get what I deserve someday,
make sure you come watch.

419
00:34:14,828 --> 00:34:16,511
Can I blow my nose?

420
00:34:28,953 --> 00:34:31,200
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

421
00:34:33,955 --> 00:34:36,138
Here are your marinated short ribs.

422
00:34:36,648 --> 00:34:38,515
How did you like the sirloin?

423
00:34:39,340 --> 00:34:40,792
It's really delicious.

424
00:34:41,329 --> 00:34:43,864
Thank you. Enjoy your meal.

425
00:34:55,267 --> 00:34:56,401
Gyu Rim.

426
00:34:58,427 --> 00:35:00,440
Gyu Yeong, Gyu O.

427
00:35:07,595 --> 00:35:09,499
Gyu Rim, Gyu Yeong, Gyu O.

428
00:35:15,215 --> 00:35:16,695
Look at you.

429
00:35:19,135 --> 00:35:20,690
Have you been going hungry?

430
00:35:22,515 --> 00:35:24,595
Haven't you been eating properly?

431
00:35:26,988 --> 00:35:28,834
Was your stepmom mean to you?

432
00:35:30,136 --> 00:35:32,545
Did your stepmom not feed you properly?

433
00:35:36,561 --> 00:35:38,522
Let's go inside and eat.

434
00:35:39,061 --> 00:35:41,161
I'll grill some meat for you.

435
00:35:42,514 --> 00:35:45,911
I'll grill the meat just right for you.

436
00:36:32,814 --> 00:36:34,928
What did you do to my kids?

437
00:36:35,295 --> 00:36:37,268
Did you feed them properly?

438
00:36:37,702 --> 00:36:39,348
Did you dress them properly?

439
00:36:40,075 --> 00:36:43,053
Did you support them
while they struggled with school?

440
00:36:43,135 --> 00:36:45,187
Did you treat them differently
from your own kids?

441
00:36:46,775 --> 00:36:49,301
You should've done better
because you didn't give birth to them.

442
00:36:49,938 --> 00:36:52,334
Because you didn't give birth to them,
you should've cared for them more,

443
00:36:52,359 --> 00:36:54,995
loved them more,
and looked after them more.

444
00:36:56,202 --> 00:37:01,445
You should've cherished them even more
because they'd lost their mom,

445
00:37:01,586 --> 00:37:05,168
and worked yourself to the bone for them.

446
00:37:05,588 --> 00:37:10,764
That's why I gave up my place
as their mom to you!

447
00:37:11,775 --> 00:37:12,775
My ears hurt.

448
00:37:13,316 --> 00:37:17,508
Let me talk too!
What are you, a machine gun?

449
00:37:19,395 --> 00:37:23,814
I didn't play favorites
between your kids and mine,

450
00:37:23,839 --> 00:37:27,005
but I didn't treat them equally either.
So what?

451
00:37:27,155 --> 00:37:30,379
What did you ever do for your kids
to be shouting like this?

452
00:37:31,009 --> 00:37:32,895
You cut off contact for 17 years,

453
00:37:32,897 --> 00:37:35,207
never called once.
Do you call that a mother?

454
00:37:35,329 --> 00:37:37,068
You have no right to do this.

455
00:37:37,093 --> 00:37:39,208
No right to come at me.

456
00:37:40,069 --> 00:37:43,235
Talk about the pot
calling the kettle black!

457
00:37:48,587 --> 00:37:52,541
I shouldn't have given her my number.
She's no help at all.

458
00:38:21,674 --> 00:38:23,405
The udon here is good.

459
00:38:24,475 --> 00:38:26,338
You'll feel better after you eat.

460
00:38:30,122 --> 00:38:33,285
Mom told me we're the same age.

461
00:38:33,908 --> 00:38:36,015
Really? We're the same age?

462
00:38:36,301 --> 00:38:38,499
But you seem so much more grown-up.

463
00:38:39,001 --> 00:38:40,613
I'm basically a little kid.

464
00:38:41,929 --> 00:38:46,036
Maybe it's because I've been through
just about everything.

465
00:38:47,732 --> 00:38:48,963
Thank you.

466
00:38:57,008 --> 00:38:58,008
Eat up.

467
00:39:03,654 --> 00:39:08,210
I think I kind of get
why Mu Jin likes you so much.

468
00:39:12,061 --> 00:39:17,391
I'm not close with Mu Jin.
I just sort of know him.

469
00:39:19,101 --> 00:39:21,410
But I've heard about you so much,
my ears hurt.

470
00:39:41,234 --> 00:39:43,977
About that time, seven years ago,

471
00:39:45,702 --> 00:39:49,570
can I ask why you called my mom?

472
00:40:15,004 --> 00:40:16,515
My baby died.

473
00:40:18,578 --> 00:40:19,795
Right after being born.

474
00:40:21,364 --> 00:40:23,089
Without ever seeing my face,

475
00:40:24,137 --> 00:40:26,508
without even getting to say goodbye to me.

476
00:40:34,294 --> 00:40:36,363
As I held my cold little baby,

477
00:40:38,815 --> 00:40:41,315
I suddenly missed my mom.

478
00:40:44,325 --> 00:40:47,906
I wanted to sleep in my mom's warm arms
for just a little while,

479
00:40:48,425 --> 00:40:50,241
so I called her.

480
00:41:24,373 --> 00:41:27,334
- This is special treatment, right?
- Totally special treatment.

481
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:31,585
I'm cooking for you and serving you
myself on my break.

482
00:41:31,610 --> 00:41:34,495
I wouldn't even do this for the president.

483
00:41:35,888 --> 00:41:38,188
- Thanks for the food.
- Hold on.

484
00:41:45,172 --> 00:41:46,335
Enjoy.

485
00:41:49,635 --> 00:41:51,962
- Mu Jin.
- Yeah.

486
00:41:53,069 --> 00:41:58,632
I'm going to be a good grown-up
when I grow up too. Like you and Mom.

487
00:42:00,495 --> 00:42:02,439
I still have a long way to go,

488
00:42:03,182 --> 00:42:05,518
so just keep taking after your mom.

489
00:42:06,029 --> 00:42:09,835
- Your mom's my role model too.
- Okay.

490
00:42:11,874 --> 00:42:16,907
But Grandpa told me to ask you
when I see you.

491
00:42:17,108 --> 00:42:20,717
- Sure.
- When will I become Kim Gyeol?

492
00:42:23,788 --> 00:42:25,049
Tell me about it.

493
00:42:25,756 --> 00:42:29,526
I want that more than world peace,

494
00:42:30,658 --> 00:42:34,952
so later, let's sit down with your mom
and have a serious talk, the three of us.

495
00:42:35,194 --> 00:42:36,293
Okay.

496
00:42:58,120 --> 00:43:00,900
(Mom)

497
00:43:03,581 --> 00:43:04,927
Hi, Mom.

498
00:43:06,685 --> 00:43:08,481
How's Dad doing?

499
00:43:09,709 --> 00:43:10,881
And my brother?

500
00:43:14,078 --> 00:43:15,362
That's a relief.

501
00:43:16,252 --> 00:43:19,228
Either way, rehab is what matters most.
You know that, right?

502
00:43:19,929 --> 00:43:21,970
Tell him not to skip it.

503
00:43:29,375 --> 00:43:30,686
And, Mom.

504
00:43:33,560 --> 00:43:34,835
You trust me, right?

505
00:43:39,233 --> 00:43:43,741
Whatever choice or decision I make,

506
00:43:44,621 --> 00:43:45,914
you'll trust me no matter what, right?

507
00:43:50,565 --> 00:43:51,817
Then that's all I need.

508
00:43:53,817 --> 00:43:56,033
As long as you trust me,
everything's fine.

509
00:44:01,408 --> 00:44:05,389
I found a man I don't want to lose
even if it kills me,

510
00:44:06,071 --> 00:44:07,949
so I'm thinking of just
grabbing hold of him.

511
00:44:08,995 --> 00:44:11,088
I'm scared someone will steal him away,

512
00:44:13,308 --> 00:44:14,974
so I'm going to hold on to him tight.

513
00:44:23,421 --> 00:44:25,254
- Yeah.
- Here's our business card.

514
00:44:25,982 --> 00:44:27,895
- Yeah.
- Thank you. Have a good day.

515
00:44:29,035 --> 00:44:31,586
Su Chan says he'll watch the store,
so I can go without worrying.

516
00:44:33,467 --> 00:44:34,467
Okay.

517
00:44:36,588 --> 00:44:38,228
I'll head out in ten minutes.

518
00:44:39,159 --> 00:44:40,159
Hold on.

519
00:44:41,662 --> 00:44:43,621
Let's meet in front of the district office
in an hour.

520
00:44:46,282 --> 00:44:48,209
Okay.

521
00:44:50,575 --> 00:44:53,629
Su Chan, Hui Na says she'll be
forever grateful to you.

522
00:44:59,322 --> 00:45:00,322
Gyu O.

523
00:45:01,569 --> 00:45:05,223
Yun Gi just sent me this.

524
00:45:05,637 --> 00:45:06,831
Take a look.

525
00:45:07,548 --> 00:45:08,548
What is it?

526
00:45:13,309 --> 00:45:15,122
Which bastard posted this?

527
00:45:16,295 --> 00:45:17,648
Do you have any idea who it was?

528
00:45:44,022 --> 00:45:46,189
I heard you married
that con-artist gigolo.

529
00:45:46,502 --> 00:45:50,215
That you knew he was a criminal
and fooled around with him anyway?

530
00:45:50,442 --> 00:45:51,762
And then you even married him?

531
00:45:52,201 --> 00:45:55,574
A schoolteacher,
who's supposed to set an example?

532
00:45:56,334 --> 00:45:58,892
With that innocent face of yours,

533
00:45:59,484 --> 00:46:02,695
does your school know?
Do the parents know?

534
00:46:04,192 --> 00:46:06,760
From a sneaky woman like you,

535
00:46:06,762 --> 00:46:10,008
what are growing kids supposed to learn?

536
00:46:17,161 --> 00:46:19,027
(Principal)

537
00:46:23,408 --> 00:46:24,908
Yes, sir.

538
00:46:28,013 --> 00:46:30,209
I'm on my way home from work.

539
00:46:31,611 --> 00:46:32,888
Right now?

540
00:46:33,662 --> 00:46:36,796
I have something urgent right now...

541
00:46:42,968 --> 00:46:48,095
Yes, it's true that I got married,
but that isn't true...

542
00:47:41,674 --> 00:47:44,235
- Can I come in?
- Don't come in!

543
00:47:44,260 --> 00:47:45,433
I'm coming in.

544
00:47:48,574 --> 00:47:50,607
What? Did you fall off the bed?

545
00:47:53,741 --> 00:47:56,151
Why is this bed so narrow?

546
00:47:56,176 --> 00:47:58,875
Rich people all use king-size beds,
even when they sleep alone.

547
00:47:59,128 --> 00:48:00,428
Don't you have any money?

548
00:48:00,475 --> 00:48:02,602
Then again, what money
would a jobless bum have?

549
00:48:02,629 --> 00:48:04,182
Want me to buy you a king-size bed?

550
00:48:04,207 --> 00:48:08,115
Now you're even picking fights
about my bed?

551
00:48:08,515 --> 00:48:12,022
At this rate, you'll be sticking flowers
in your hair in no time.

552
00:48:13,279 --> 00:48:16,074
My head's about to explode,
and I feel like I'm losing it,

553
00:48:16,099 --> 00:48:19,268
so if I really do lose it,
just dump me on some deserted island,

554
00:48:19,293 --> 00:48:21,032
so nobody finds out I've lost my mind.

555
00:48:21,828 --> 00:48:24,624
Just change your clothes.
Let's go out and clear your head.

556
00:48:25,231 --> 00:48:28,229
Forget it. I'm scared to see people.

557
00:48:29,042 --> 00:48:31,535
Then just make sure nobody knows
you're Han Gyu Yeong.

558
00:48:31,560 --> 00:48:33,179
How am I supposed to do that?

559
00:48:33,383 --> 00:48:36,285
Even in jeans and a T-shirt,
my face just glows.

560
00:48:36,310 --> 00:48:37,714
Every guy turns to look.

561
00:48:37,739 --> 00:48:40,039
You've really got it bad.

562
00:48:47,841 --> 00:48:49,035
Pretty.

563
00:48:52,955 --> 00:48:54,524
Heung Sik!

564
00:49:06,128 --> 00:49:08,319
He told me to wait a sec,
so why isn't he coming?

565
00:49:08,344 --> 00:49:10,110
What if Kang Seong Uk shows up?

566
00:49:11,709 --> 00:49:13,814
Go ahead and show up, you bastard.

567
00:49:13,909 --> 00:49:17,008
Who do you think you're threatening,
you sewer maggot?

568
00:49:28,622 --> 00:49:30,909
Granny. Get in, Granny.

569
00:49:33,208 --> 00:49:35,808
- Heung Sik?
- Get in, quick.

570
00:49:40,615 --> 00:49:42,733
It'll be a hassle if people recognize me.
Hurry, get in.

571
00:49:43,054 --> 00:49:46,034
What is this?
What's with this car and this look?

572
00:49:46,169 --> 00:49:50,310
This is my car.
And this is my official look for work.

573
00:49:50,385 --> 00:49:52,048
Happy? Just get in.

574
00:49:53,468 --> 00:49:55,480
What is all this? Are you a spy?

575
00:49:55,561 --> 00:49:57,268
Undercover? A shadow figure?

576
00:49:58,142 --> 00:49:59,435
And what about Su Nam?

577
00:49:59,485 --> 00:50:02,277
Is she on your team too?
Posing as mother and son?

578
00:50:02,302 --> 00:50:05,569
Stop imagining nonsense and get in.
You'll see when we get there.

579
00:50:05,594 --> 00:50:08,814
- You sure talk a lot.
- How much did you rake in...

580
00:50:08,975 --> 00:50:10,858
to be this rich?

581
00:50:11,702 --> 00:50:14,408
What kind of work? What work do you do?

582
00:50:14,635 --> 00:50:16,055
It's related to national security.

583
00:50:16,082 --> 00:50:18,964
Why? Going to report me for a reward?

584
00:50:19,125 --> 00:50:21,166
Just get in. You'll see when we get there.

585
00:50:21,235 --> 00:50:23,905
- You sure talk a lot.
- Where are we going?

586
00:50:24,382 --> 00:50:27,357
- People are watching.
- Who's watching?

587
00:50:52,301 --> 00:50:55,698
You're quite the handsome model.

588
00:50:56,302 --> 00:50:57,462
Heung Sik.

589
00:50:58,862 --> 00:51:02,851
I'm Joel, today's photographer.

590
00:51:03,932 --> 00:51:09,414
Surprised? Let's do a good job,
Han Gyu Seo. I'm counting on you.

591
00:51:12,099 --> 00:51:16,341
Heung Sik, where should I seat
the guest you brought?

592
00:51:17,322 --> 00:51:18,741
No need to seat her.

593
00:51:18,822 --> 00:51:21,261
She'll find some corner on her own.

594
00:51:21,935 --> 00:51:22,981
Good.

595
00:51:45,035 --> 00:51:46,315
Lee Guk.

596
00:51:47,368 --> 00:51:48,368
Let's see.

597
00:51:48,815 --> 00:51:50,595
- This is today's concept, okay?
- Okay.

598
00:51:56,257 --> 00:52:00,142
Sit like this and use it like this.

599
00:52:00,167 --> 00:52:02,936
- I do it with this product?
- Yep, that's right.

600
00:52:38,045 --> 00:52:39,048
Nice.

601
00:52:39,276 --> 00:52:41,327
Look, it's good.

602
00:52:43,354 --> 00:52:45,448
It's so good.

603
00:52:46,345 --> 00:52:48,712
Our model.

604
00:52:48,755 --> 00:52:53,408
Your skin looks amazing right now,
and you've been doing great already,

605
00:52:53,755 --> 00:52:58,035
but let's really bring out
the cream's dewy finish in the photos.

606
00:52:58,060 --> 00:53:00,146
- One more time.
- Okay.

607
00:53:18,554 --> 00:53:20,761
What should I do with these?

608
00:53:21,128 --> 00:53:24,128
You set some aside for me
before you even sold them?

609
00:53:24,841 --> 00:53:28,434
These are Geumyeong Bay oysters
from down near my hometown.

610
00:53:28,875 --> 00:53:32,308
I thought of you, so I brought a few.

611
00:53:32,346 --> 00:53:35,452
That's not a few. That's a lot.

612
00:53:36,662 --> 00:53:40,302
The shells are big, but once shucked,
there's really not that much.

613
00:53:40,304 --> 00:53:45,908
My goodness, Geumyeong Bay oysters
are really something.

614
00:53:46,129 --> 00:53:49,689
I'm still this full of energy,

615
00:53:49,714 --> 00:53:53,506
because I ate lots of oysters
when I was young.

616
00:53:53,608 --> 00:53:59,208
And my skin's this good
because of oysters too.

617
00:53:59,210 --> 00:54:00,713
Of course.

618
00:54:01,199 --> 00:54:05,704
I can't eat this much all by myself,

619
00:54:05,947 --> 00:54:10,848
and there's someone
I really want to share it with.

620
00:54:10,914 --> 00:54:12,474
Share as much as you like.

621
00:54:12,529 --> 00:54:14,595
They're yours now.

622
00:54:15,110 --> 00:54:20,761
Gyu Rim is just crazy about oysters.

623
00:54:22,668 --> 00:54:25,582
And I feel a little
guilty toward her, too.

624
00:54:27,631 --> 00:54:33,409
Would you be hurt if I gave
all of these to her?

625
00:54:33,442 --> 00:54:37,415
It doesn't bother me at all.

626
00:54:37,422 --> 00:54:39,977
They're yours, and you want to give them,

627
00:54:40,095 --> 00:54:43,974
and on top of that,
these oysters are going to Gyu Rim.

628
00:54:44,048 --> 00:54:46,169
If a certain someone found that out,

629
00:54:46,463 --> 00:54:51,268
he'd be super happy.

630
00:54:51,461 --> 00:54:53,174
Who? Who's that?

631
00:54:53,210 --> 00:54:56,402
My neck hurts, so sit down and let's talk.

632
00:54:56,714 --> 00:54:58,397
Who'd be super happy?

633
00:54:59,598 --> 00:55:02,078
(Imsang Seafood)

634
00:55:24,708 --> 00:55:26,721
Tell me I'm in my right mind.

635
00:55:28,729 --> 00:55:30,189
You're in your right mind.

636
00:55:31,515 --> 00:55:33,622
Tell me I'm not wrong.

637
00:55:34,022 --> 00:55:35,582
You're not wrong.

638
00:55:36,402 --> 00:55:39,302
Tell me I'm not crazy.

639
00:55:39,609 --> 00:55:41,435
You're not crazy.

640
00:55:42,154 --> 00:55:43,667
But how long are we doing this?

641
00:55:44,256 --> 00:55:46,609
It's not like it's
a listen-and-repeat test.

642
00:55:50,836 --> 00:55:52,689
What will you do if I am crazy?

643
00:55:53,227 --> 00:55:56,008
- What?
- What if I'm wrong?

644
00:55:57,914 --> 00:55:58,934
What?

645
00:55:59,016 --> 00:56:02,269
What will you do if I'm wrong and crazy?

646
00:56:04,996 --> 00:56:06,602
I'll still hang out with you.

647
00:56:09,042 --> 00:56:12,511
Even if you're wrong,
even if you're crazy,

648
00:56:13,524 --> 00:56:17,160
and people curse you
and point fingers at you,

649
00:56:17,549 --> 00:56:19,428
and no one will hang out with you,

650
00:56:22,588 --> 00:56:24,415
I'll keep hanging out with you.

651
00:56:30,328 --> 00:56:34,234
But you know what's really strange?

652
00:56:36,848 --> 00:56:39,528
You keep making me a good person.

653
00:56:40,775 --> 00:56:42,188
When I'm with you,

654
00:56:44,821 --> 00:56:46,842
I keep turning into a good person.

655
00:56:56,693 --> 00:57:00,479
You promised.

656
00:57:02,127 --> 00:57:04,903
Even if everyone curses me
and points fingers at me,

657
00:57:04,928 --> 00:57:07,785
and no one hangs out with me, you...

658
00:57:11,027 --> 00:57:15,881
You'll hang out with me, right?

659
00:57:51,715 --> 00:57:54,622
Why is she so out of it?

660
00:57:57,114 --> 00:58:00,701
Could she have found out?

661
00:58:05,348 --> 00:58:08,642
- Gyu Rim.
- Yes, Su Nam.

662
00:58:08,667 --> 00:58:11,914
How could you not even hear
someone coming in?

663
00:58:12,529 --> 00:58:13,809
Did something happen?

664
00:58:14,741 --> 00:58:18,415
No, nothing happened. I'm sorry.

665
00:58:18,440 --> 00:58:22,013
I'm the one who should be sorry to you.

666
00:58:22,321 --> 00:58:23,342
Excuse me?

667
00:58:23,668 --> 00:58:28,368
No, it's nothing.
I brought you some oysters.

668
00:58:28,442 --> 00:58:31,088
You're crazy about oysters, aren't you?

669
00:58:31,142 --> 00:58:33,082
This many?

670
00:58:33,642 --> 00:58:35,750
Just a few would've been fine.

671
00:58:35,775 --> 00:58:39,570
I suddenly developed an oyster allergy,

672
00:58:39,595 --> 00:58:43,078
so just looking at the box makes me itch.

673
00:58:43,261 --> 00:58:45,461
Eat all of it yourself.

674
00:58:45,948 --> 00:58:47,261
Su Nam.

675
00:58:50,868 --> 00:58:56,108
You're the type who'd jump out of bed
for oysters.

676
00:58:56,534 --> 00:59:01,194
You just never make a fuss
and always let others go first.

677
00:59:01,875 --> 00:59:05,695
So don't give any of these to anyone.

678
00:59:05,722 --> 00:59:09,435
Not your dad, not your siblings,
not even Gyeol.

679
00:59:09,728 --> 00:59:13,288
Eat every last one yourself, okay?

680
00:59:13,696 --> 00:59:15,369
I'll come and check.

681
00:59:17,481 --> 00:59:19,478
Aren't you going to answer?

682
00:59:21,514 --> 00:59:24,064
You need at least one thing in your life,

683
00:59:25,092 --> 00:59:29,326
just for you,
without thinking about anyone else.

684
00:59:32,321 --> 00:59:36,301
Okay. I'll eat it all myself.

685
00:59:37,035 --> 00:59:41,346
- I'll make sure I eat it all myself.
- Enjoy every bite.

686
01:00:39,735 --> 01:00:40,761
Hey.

687
01:00:41,968 --> 01:00:43,568
Are these the oysters that came in today?

688
01:00:43,907 --> 01:00:45,474
I definitely tasted them.

689
01:00:48,535 --> 01:00:50,781
No. We can't serve these oysters today.

690
01:00:51,248 --> 01:00:55,361
Throw out all of today's oysters
and tell Park Jeong Woo to come down.

691
01:00:55,386 --> 01:00:56,406
Yes.

692
01:01:10,841 --> 01:01:13,764
No.

693
01:01:18,135 --> 01:01:20,635
Secretary Ahn,
I don't think this is right.

694
01:01:20,660 --> 01:01:22,111
Cancel everything I told you to do.

695
01:01:22,136 --> 01:01:24,148
I wasn't in my right mind.

696
01:01:25,234 --> 01:01:30,095
I was crazy. I completely lost it.

697
01:01:46,302 --> 01:01:48,625
What do you mean,
don't take orders from customers?

698
01:01:48,656 --> 01:01:50,882
And why? Is there a problem?

699
01:01:50,928 --> 01:01:53,950
Tell Mr. Im at Geumyeong Bay
I'm going to kill him,

700
01:01:54,185 --> 01:01:55,512
and tell the customers...

701
01:01:57,132 --> 01:01:59,781
honestly that we can't serve the oysters
because there's a problem with them.

702
01:02:00,401 --> 01:02:04,261
And a bottle of wine for those
who came just for the oysters...

703
01:02:04,286 --> 01:02:05,468
No.

704
01:02:05,968 --> 01:02:08,622
Give every customer tonight
a bottle of wine on the house.

705
01:02:08,647 --> 01:02:11,220
Didn't I tell you
money doesn't grow on trees?

706
01:02:11,415 --> 01:02:12,993
Do you really want to go under?

707
01:02:13,018 --> 01:02:15,932
If going under is your goal, just say so.
There are much easier ways.

708
01:02:15,957 --> 01:02:19,353
I'll pay for the wine myself,
so save the nagging for texts.

709
01:02:21,781 --> 01:02:23,754
A customer is asking for you, sir.

710
01:02:25,067 --> 01:02:26,727
Let's get moving for now.

711
01:02:29,062 --> 01:02:30,221
Mu Jin.

712
01:02:31,475 --> 01:02:34,095
Gyu Rim might have eaten them.

713
01:02:36,220 --> 01:02:40,602
I'm telling you,
those oysters went to Gyu Rim.

714
01:03:26,600 --> 01:03:29,266
(Love on the Menu)

715
01:03:29,291 --> 01:03:31,667
Who could it be?
Who would go this far against me?

716
01:03:31,692 --> 01:03:34,629
- Sit.
- From now on, don't trust me or anyone.

717
01:03:34,654 --> 01:03:37,687
If there's someone behind this,
don't tell me.

718
01:03:37,712 --> 01:03:39,679
I should've taken them with me.

719
01:03:39,704 --> 01:03:41,529
Please punish me.

720
01:03:41,702 --> 01:03:44,310
Punish me for leaving my kids behind.

721
01:03:44,523 --> 01:03:47,548
You can curse me or blame me,

722
01:03:47,573 --> 01:03:49,022
so just say whatever you want.

723
01:03:49,047 --> 01:03:51,812
I came because I was scared.
I was afraid I'd do something crazy.

724
01:03:51,881 --> 01:03:54,645
Gyu Rim, can't we just cut ties?

725
01:03:55,969 --> 01:03:57,769
Dramaday.me
